BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 790 Tm (- TD3 is basically a more robust DDPG family method. It still gives a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 777 Tm (  deterministic continuous actor, which is convenient for deployment as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 764 Tm (  current-command policy. The two critics, delayed policy updates, and target) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 751 Tm (  smoothing directly address the DDPG failure mode.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 734 Tm (- SAC is also off-policy and continuous, but the actor is stochastic during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 721 Tm (  training and it optimizes reward plus entropy. That can make exploration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 708 Tm (  better, especially for swing-up, but it changes more assumptions and usually) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 695 Tm (  uses a larger stochastic policy. It remains a good future option.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 678 Tm (- PPO is different: it is on-policy. It collects trajectories with the current) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 665 Tm (  policy and then updates within a clipped/trust-region-like objective so the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 652 Tm (  policy does not change too violently. PPO can handle discrete or continuous) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 639 Tm (  actions. In the Brian Douglas/QUBE hybrid example, PPO is used for discrete) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 626 Tm (  mode selection, not for motor current directly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 609 Tm (Good concise line:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 591 Tm (> DDPG failed first, TD3 was the closest controlled improvement, SAC was a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 577 Tm (> reasonable future alternative, and PPO fit the hybrid switching problem more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 563 Tm (> than our direct continuous-current controller.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 539 Tm (Slide 5 - Observation And Action Design) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 516 Tm (This is one of the important lessons:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 498 Tm (> For swing-up, raw wrapped angles are awkward because the pendulum error jumps) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 484 Tm (> at the wrap boundary. Using sine and cosine gives the policy a continuous) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 470 Tm (> global angle representation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 453 Tm (Mention that `previousAction` was added because:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 436 Tm (- action-difference is in the reward,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 423 Tm (- actuator dynamics make the previous command relevant,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 410 Tm (- it helps the observation be closer to Markov.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 386 Tm (Slide 6 - Early Attempts And Lessons) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 363 Tm (Frame early failures as useful:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 345 Tm (> The early DDPG and TD3 attempts were not wasted. They revealed that training) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 331 Tm (> reward was not enough, raw local observations were insufficient for swing-up,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 317 Tm (> and in-episode learning could make Simulink training very expensive.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 300 Tm (Mention learning frequency:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 283 Tm (- DDPG initially learned very frequently,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 270 Tm (- TD3 update cost became large when episodes survived longer,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 257 Tm (- `LearningFrequency = -1` moved learning to episode end.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 233 Tm (Slide 7 - Key Shift: MathWorks-Style TD3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 210 Tm (This is the first big success point.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 193 Tm (Explain:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 176 Tm (- no curriculum at first,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 163 Tm (- fixed broad reset,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 150 Tm (- fixed evaluation grid,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 137 Tm (- episode-end learning,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 124 Tm (- default 64-64 actor/critic style.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 107 Tm (Important phrasing:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 89 Tm (> The MathWorks-style setup did not magically solve RL. It made the experiment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 75 Tm (> clean enough that TD3 could learn and that the evaluation became meaningful.) Tj ET
endstream
