BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 690 Tm (500 Hz PI/current long:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 673 Tm (- closer to hardware deployment,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 660 Tm (- corrected evaluation after sample-time workspace bug,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 647 Tm (- best hardware candidate so far.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 630 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 612 Tm (> This 500 Hz long policy is the one that became the main hardware-tested) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 598 Tm (> policy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 574 Tm (Slide 8b - 500 Hz Long Training Config) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 551 Tm (Use this slide if someone asks what "500 Hz long" actually means.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 534 Tm (The important distinction is that there are two time scales:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 517 Tm (- the plant simulation still ran at `5e-5 s`, so the model/PI loop side was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 504 Tm (  effectively 20 kHz,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 491 Tm (- the RL policy only chose a new action every `0.002 s`, so the agent acted at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 478 Tm (  500 Hz.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 461 Tm (For one training episode:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 444 Tm (EpisodeDuration / AgentSampleTime = 5 s / 0.002 s = 2500 agent steps) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 429 Tm (That means a full-length episode gives 2500 transitions to the replay buffer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 416 Tm (An episode can end earlier if the Simulink `isDone` logic trips, for example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 403 Tm (because the arm or pendulum leaves the allowed training envelope. For hardware,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 390 Tm (we may tolerate small boundary violations more carefully, but during training) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 377 Tm (`isDone` matters because it shapes what the agent thinks is terminal failure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 360 Tm (Explain the learning settings plainly:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 343 Tm (- `LearningFrequency = -1` means MATLAB does not update the neural networks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 330 Tm (  every few agent steps during the episode. It collects the episode, then runs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 317 Tm (  learning at the end.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 304 Tm (- `MiniBatchSize = 1024` means each gradient update samples 1024 transitions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 291 Tm (  from the replay buffer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 278 Tm (- `NumEpoch = 10` means the end-of-episode learning pass can repeat for 10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 265 Tm (  epochs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 252 Tm (- `MaxMiniBatchPerEpoch = 100` limits each epoch to at most 100 minibatches.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 235 Tm (So the maximum number of minibatch updates over the full configured run is:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 218 Tm (MaxEpisodes * NumEpoch * MaxMiniBatchPerEpoch) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 207 Tm (= 5000 * 10 * 100) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 196 Tm (= 5,000,000 minibatch updates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 181 Tm (This is an upper bound. Actual work can be lower if the replay buffer is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 168 Tm (ready early on, if episodes terminate quickly, or if MATLAB internally stops a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 155 Tm (learning pass because there is not enough useful data. It is also not the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 142 Tm (as environment steps. The maximum environment interaction is:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 125 Tm (5000 episodes * 2500 steps = 12,500,000 agent steps) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 110 Tm (In TD3, the critic is updated more often than the actor. With) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 97 Tm (`PolicyUpdateFrequency = 2`, the actor update is delayed and only happens every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 84 Tm (second critic-update step. This is one of the reasons TD3 is usually more stable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 71 Tm (than plain DDPG.) Tj ET
endstream
