BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 790 Tm (- smaller network,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 777 Tm (- reduced observation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 764 Tm (- detailed model,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 751 Tm (- state-dependent reward,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 738 Tm (- domain randomization later.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 721 Tm (Then give the outcomes. This is a useful "we actually tested the advice" slide:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 704 Tm (1. Smaller network:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 687 Tm (- Actor 1x64 / critic 1x64 failed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 674 Tm (- It mostly failed by barely acting, so it was probably underfit or the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 661 Tm (     critic was too weak.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 648 Tm (- Actor 1x64 / critic 2x64 learned. So the small actor idea was viable, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 635 Tm (     the critic needed capacity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 622 Tm (- It was not the new hardware candidate because balance metrics were worse.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 605 Tm (2. Reduced observation:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 588 Tm (- Pure unsigned arc distance was elegant but removed direction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 575 Tm (- The run failed/interrupted and was still terminating after tens of steps.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 562 Tm (- Lesson: one scalar per angle is attractive, but not if it makes left/right) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 549 Tm (     or positive/negative error ambiguous.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 532 Tm (3. Detailed model:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 515 Tm (- This was the most valuable path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 502 Tm (- It added current noise, friction, filters, encoder effects, current PI) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 489 Tm (     behavior, and dead-zone compensation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 476 Tm (- The first result was not better control, but it exposed the real next) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 463 Tm (     problem: the old reward can learn survival/swinging instead of capture.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 446 Tm (4. Domain randomization:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 429 Tm (- Initially attractive after hardware mismatch.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 416 Tm (- Paused deliberately because the nominal detailed model still does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 403 Tm (     learn clean capture.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 386 Tm (Transition:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 368 Tm (> Weto's input helped turn the project from "try more training" into controlled) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 354 Tm (> experiments: network, observation, detailed model, then reward and robustness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 330 Tm (Slide 12b - Why Not The Brian Douglas Hybrid SAC/PPO Route?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 307 Tm (This is worth explaining because it is a very reasonable question.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 290 Tm (The Brian Douglas / MathWorks QUBE Servo2 reference uses a hybrid architecture:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 273 Tm (- classical feedback controller handles upright balance,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 260 Tm (- SAC learns swing-up behavior/reference generation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 247 Tm (- PPO chooses the mode, essentially switching between swing-up and the balance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 234 Tm (  controller.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 217 Tm (Why this is attractive:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 200 Tm (- it uses classical control where classical control is strong,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 187 Tm (- it gives RL a narrower job,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 174 Tm (- it avoids asking one neural policy to solve swing-up, capture, and stable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 161 Tm (  balance all at once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 144 Tm (Why we did not follow it directly:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 127 Tm (1. Project objective.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 110 Tm (   The goal here was to explore whether a direct RL controller could learn the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 97 Tm (   Furuta swing-up/balance task and transfer to hardware. If we used a classical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 84 Tm (   controller for balance from the start, the final result would be less about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 71 Tm (   direct RL control and more about RL-assisted switching.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
14 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 595 842] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 15 0 R >>
endobj
15 0 obj
<< /Length 4031 >>
stream
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 790 Tm (2. Integration complexity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 773 Tm (   The Brian Douglas example is built for Quanser QUBE/Raspberry Pi and its own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 760 Tm (   Simulink architecture. Our setup uses the ZHAW Furuta model, SLDRT, UART, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 747 Tm (   microcontroller current PI loop, and different hardware signals. Porting the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 734 Tm (   full hybrid architecture would be a project by itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 717 Tm (3. Debuggability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 700 Tm (   The hybrid design has at least three moving pieces: SAC swing-up, PPO mode) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 687 Tm (   selector, and classical balance controller. Early in our project, we were) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 674 Tm (   still debugging signs, reward, sample time, evaluation, and actuator) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 661 Tm (   interface. A direct TD3 baseline was easier to diagnose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 644 Tm (4. Controlled algorithm path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 627 Tm (   We started with DDPG. TD3 was the smallest algorithmic step that addressed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 614 Tm (   DDPG's known weakness while keeping the same deterministic continuous-action) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 601 Tm (   framing. SAC/PPO would have changed more at once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 584 Tm (Fair conclusion:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 566 Tm (> The hybrid SAC/PPO architecture is probably a strong future fallback or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 552 Tm (> extension. In hindsight, it also supports one lesson from our work: swing-up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 538 Tm (> and balance may deserve different controllers, rewards, or modes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 514 Tm (Slide 13 - Smaller Network Experiments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 491 Tm (Important nuance:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 473 Tm (> A smaller actor is feasible, but a too-small critic failed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 456 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 439 Tm (- actor 1x64 / critic 1x64 did not act enough,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 426 Tm (- actor 1x64 / critic 2x64 learned,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 413 Tm (- but it was not better for upright balance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 396 Tm (Lesson:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 378 Tm (> Critic capacity matters during training even if we want a small deployed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 364 Tm (> actor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 340 Tm (Slide 14 - Reduced Observation Experiments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 317 Tm (Explain the topology tradeoff:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 299 Tm (> For a circular angle, one scalar cannot be globally continuous, directional,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 285 Tm (> and compact at the same time. We tried an unsigned arc-distance scalar, but it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 271 Tm (> lost too much directional information.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 254 Tm (Main lesson:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 236 Tm (> Smaller observation is not automatically better. The policy needs the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 222 Tm (> information required to choose direction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 198 Tm (Slide 15 - Detailed Model Work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 175 Tm (This slide is about engineering realism.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 158 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 140 Tm (> The simple model was useful for learning, but hardware has friction,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 126 Tm (> filtering, current-loop dynamics, quantization, and dead zones. The detailed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 112 Tm (> model tries to represent those before adding randomization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 95 Tm (Mention the principle:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 77 Tm (> Do not randomize a model that cannot solve the nominal task yet.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
