stream
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 790 Tm (Slide 20 - Handover: Repository Structure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 767 Tm (Show the repository.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 750 Tm (Point to:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 733 Tm (- `docs/` first,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 720 Tm (- `scripts/make*Config.m` for training definitions,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 707 Tm (- `scripts/train*.m` for launchers,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 694 Tm (- `scripts/analysis/` for hardware/simulation save and compare,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 681 Tm (- `results/TD3/` for runs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 668 Tm (- `results/model_vs_hardware/` for hardware data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 651 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 633 Tm (> The most important thing for continuation is to start from the documented) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 619 Tm (> baseline, not from a random latest file.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 595 Tm (Slide 21 - Demo Plan) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 572 Tm (Suggested demo if time is short:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 555 Tm (1. Open the hardware swing-up average plot.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 542 Tm (2. Open the model-vs-hardware comparison plot.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 529 Tm (3. Show the SLDRT/current command Simulink path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 516 Tm (4. Show the result folder structure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 499 Tm (If hardware is connected:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 482 Tm (- only run if safety setup is ready,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 469 Tm (- use reduced current scaling,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 456 Tm (- log the run.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 432 Tm (Slide 22 - Future Work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 409 Tm (State the recommended next step:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 391 Tm (> Do not add broad domain randomization yet. First make the nominal detailed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 377 Tm (> model capture and balance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 360 Tm (Then:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 343 Tm (- capture-tune latest 1c detailed agent,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 330 Tm (- add upright-region shaping,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 317 Tm (- use policy-preserving fine-tuning,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 304 Tm (- add actuator state if needed,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 291 Tm (- then domain randomization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 267 Tm (Slide 22b - Sim-To-Real Research Directions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 244 Tm (Connect this back to the current state:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 226 Tm (> We now have a policy that works on the simpler model and transfers partly to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 212 Tm (> hardware, but detailed-model fine-tuning can damage it. That makes this a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 198 Tm (> sim-to-real adaptation problem, not just a "train longer" problem.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 181 Tm (Summarize the papers/ideas:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 164 Tm (1. SimOpt / adaptive domain randomization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 147 Tm (   Instead of manually guessing friction/current/dead-zone randomization ranges) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 134 Tm (   forever, use real rollouts to adapt the simulator distribution. This matches) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 121 Tm (   the idea of collecting hardware logs, comparing them to simulation, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 108 Tm (   tightening or shifting the randomization.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 91 Tm (2. Residual reinforcement learning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 74 Tm (   Keep a useful base controller and learn a correction. This is attractive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 61 Tm (   because the `500Hz_long` policy already has useful swing-up behavior. A) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
